 "title": "Marriage Records - Recorder's Office - Johnson County",
 "text": "Marriage Records - Recorder's Office - Johnson County\nSkip to main content\nMeetings and Agendas\nCounty News\nEvent Calendar\nI Need To\nApply for a grant or submit a bid\nFind County contact information\nFill out a form\nFind a job\nGet a free gun lock\nGet a permit\nPay court fines\nPay taxes or fees\nRegister a vehicle\nRenew my driver's license\nRequest public records\nServe jury duty\nCounty Groups\nDepartment Directory & Resources\nSearch\n-->\nMarriage Records\nHome\nForms and Fees\nDocument Formatting\nState Certified Copies\nLinks\nMilitary Discharges\nHome\n!\nNotice of Price Increase\nVITAL RECORDS INCREASE TO $20 ON JULY 1, 2026\nForms\nMarriage Record Application Form\nAttorney Proof of Entitlement\nMail Requirements\nComplete the Application form\nApplication must be NOTARIZED\nInclude copy of valid PHOTO ID\nCertified copy cost: $20\nMail To\nJohnson County Recorder\nAttn: Vital Records\n913 S Dubuque St\nIowa City, IA 52240-4273\nA vital record can also be ordered by calling: 1-866-809-0290\nPublic access to vital records is only available in the office.\nMarriage records begin at the year 1839. Certified copies are $20 and only available to entitled parties (i.e. person named on record, parents, children, spouses, siblings, grandparents). Individuals requesting a marriage record must prove entitlement by showing proper identification. Marriage events from 1954—“current day” can be issued in any county. Marriage events from 1839—1953 must be obtained through the county where the license to marry was issued.\nMarriage records between the years 1921 – 1941 must be requested through the Iowa Department of Public Health .\nNeed to talk to someone from the county?\nContact Us\nTitle VI and ADA Resources\nAbout Johnson County\nContact\nEmail subscriptions\nAmerican Rescue Plan Act\nCopyright 2019 Johnson County. All rights reserved. Iowa web design by Webspec Design.",
